KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ names a later throwing member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ names a later non-throwing member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The noexcept expression of a member declaration that cannot be evaluated
at the declaration (b is not yet declared) is kept for
implicit_exception_specifications, but the kept expression is not on the
class's component nor on the method's symbol by then, so it is never
evaluated and a() stays non-throwing (assertion 1 fails).
